# Rules to skip for specific paths in this crate.
# Format: RULE/name:path/glob — gitignore-style glob relative to crate root.
# Every entry requires a WHY: comment. No blanket category ignores.

# WHY: kryphos is the vault/crypto library. `Vault`, `VaultKey`, `SigningKey`,
# `InstallationIdentity`, etc. are re-exported from lib.rs and consumed by
# akroasis and integration tests (`tests/tamper_log_signing.rs`). Definition
# files must keep `pub` on those types and their methods for the re-exports
# to resolve (Rust E0365/E0624). The RUST/pub-visibility rule's lib.rs/mod.rs
# exemption does not reach into the defining files.
RUST/pub-visibility:src/**
